/*
 * keepsakeShapes.js — the sixteen keepsake shapes, one per region (T5.3l)
 * =============================================================================
 * Kimia's final shapes. Her rule: a keepsake is mostly a variation on a
 * section of its flora's silhouette. So most are cut from the flora's own
 * trace (floraSilhouettes.js / newFloraSilhouettes.js): a piece kept, turned,
 * shrunk or repeated, with every cut line softened so it reads as drawn, not
 * sliced. A few go further at her direction: gaba's lobes are rounded off
 * underneath, hayunti's fan slice sits in a soft drawn border, bumyaab's cap
 * sits on a drawn round fruit, siki's strip carries soft thorns, pataya's
 * petals stand on a stalk, kiyajong-ha's berries have a skin, and dalat's is
 * its outer edge with the hole filled in.
 *
 * These are finished artwork, kept verbatim like the flora traces: the code
 * only paints them. Each entry carries the region and the flora it belongs to
 * (world-building.md's table, in discovery order), the flora's shape number
 * there, and the same two fields as the flora files: `viewBox` and one path
 * `d`. They are drawn by the flora's recipe (Flora.jsx) in one of the four
 * keepsakeColours.js colours. No sizes live here: a keepsake's size is not
 * decided yet. Nothing in the game reads them yet; the drop logic comes later.
 * =========================================================================== */

